          "title": "Lambda Execution Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Lambda Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "One function run per **event**, in a managed ==execution environment==",
                "Pay per ==request== and per ==GB-second==",
                "No servers to manage"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Handler and Lifecycle",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "def handler(event, context):",
                "    left = context.get_remaining_time_in_millis()",
                "    return {\"left_ms\": left}"
              ],
              "note": "event = trigger JSON; context = request ID, time left, memory"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Init",
                    "sub": "download code, start runtime, run outside-handler code",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Invoke",
                    "sub": "run handler",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Shutdown",
                    "sub": "environment freed",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Warm environment is reused, so ==Init is skipped==",
                "Code outside the handler runs ==once per environment=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Invocation Types",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Caller waits",
                "Retries",
                "Example"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Synchronous",
                  "yes",
                  "the caller",
                  "API Gateway"
                ],
                [
                  "Asynchronous",
                  "no, queued",
                  "Lambda, **twice**",
                  "S3, SNS"
                ],
                [
                  "Event source mapping",
                  "no, polled",
                  "queue or stream",
                  "SQS, Kinesis, DynamoDB Streams"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Event to handler?** Init if cold, then Invoke.",
                "**Outside code runs once?** Init runs once; warm reuse skips it.",
                "**Who retries?** Sync: the caller. Async: Lambda, twice."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
