          "title": "When Not to Use Serverless and Common Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Poor Fit",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "Why not Lambda",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Job over 15 min",
                  "15 min timeout cap",
                  "containers"
                ],
                [
                  "Steady high load",
                  "per-request cost adds up",
                  "containers or EC2"
                ],
                [
                  "Low latency",
                  "cold starts",
                  "containers"
                ],
                [
                  "Large or GPU",
                  "10,240 MB cap, no GPU",
                  "EC2"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Function triggers itself, or two trigger each other: set ==reserved concurrency== and a **billing alarm**",
                "DB connection per invocation exhausts the DB: use ==RDS Proxy== or a pool outside the handler",
                "`/tmp` and globals may vanish: keep state in ==S3== or ==DynamoDB==",
                "Retries and SQS deliver ==at least once==: make handlers **idempotent**"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "conn = pymysql.connect(host=PROXY_HOST)",
                "",
                "def handler(event, context):",
                "    with conn.cursor() as cur:",
                "        cur.execute(\"SELECT * FROM orders WHERE id = %s\",",
                "                    (event[\"id\"],))",
                "        return cur.fetchone()"
              ],
              "note": "connect once per environment, outside the handler"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Remember",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Idempotent",
              "text": "The same event twice must give the same result. Use an ==idempotency key==, such as the order ID."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
